<title>USA: Mass. Gov expected to ink bills funding 'Big Dig'.</title>
<headline>Mass. Gov expected to ink bills funding 'Big Dig'.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Massachusetts Gov. William Weld is expected this week to sign the Metropolitan Highway System bill, the measure that supporters hope will produce the state's share of the financing for the nation's most costly construction project.</p>
<p>The proposal enlarges the Turnpike Authority to consist of the three harbor tunnels and the Tobin Bridge, as well as the Boston extention of the Massachusetts Turnpike.</p>
<p>Under the measure, the Turnpike Authority will be able to raise tolls on those arteries that will then be used to fund state bonds for the project, the $10.7 billion Central Artery/Third Harbor Tunnel or the &quot;Big Dig&quot; as it is called.</p>
<p>The expansion of the Turnpike Authority was necessary, legislators said, becasue financing experts told them that the state will be unable to ante up its 25 percent of the $5.5 billion remaining construction costs unless tolls rise.</p>
<p>((--Boston bureau, 617-367-4106))</p>
